WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.085
The framework begins by receiving the video stream, starting with frame k minus two.

2
00:00:06.085 --> 00:00:10.689
A convolutional backbone extracts visual feature representations from the frame.

3
00:00:10.689 --> 00:00:15.293
The Transformer Video Module models spatio-temporal relations using self-attention mechanisms.

4
00:00:15.293 --> 00:00:19.896
A panoptic decoder then generates the initial pixel-level panoptic segmentation.

5
00:00:19.896 --> 00:00:25.241
Initial instance identifiers are assigned to establish consistent tracking across the clip.

6
00:00:25.241 --> 00:00:30.956
For the subsequent frame k minus one, features are extracted via the backbone.

7
00:00:30.956 --> 00:00:36.670
The Transformer Video Module aggregates features across both the current and preceding frames.

8
00:00:36.670 --> 00:00:43.496
An optical flow decoder estimates motion between frames to warp the previous instance ID map forward.

9
00:00:43.496 --> 00:00:48.470
Concurrently, the panoptic decoder predicts the segmentation for the current frame.

10
00:00:48.470 --> 00:00:53.444
ID association matches the warped historical identities with current instance predictions.

11
00:00:53.444 --> 00:00:58.048
Processing continues to frame k, extracting its visual feature representations.

12
00:00:58.048 --> 00:01:03.393
The Transformer module integrates temporal context across consecutive frames in the sequence.

13
00:01:03.393 --> 00:01:09.848
Inter-frame motion is decoded to warp the tracked ID map from frame k minus one.

14
00:01:09.848 --> 00:01:14.452
The panoptic decoder yields the segmentation map for frame k.

15
00:01:14.452 --> 00:01:19.796
Finally, ID association assigns consistent tracking identifiers across the entire video sequence.

